<title>TAIWAN: China Airlines applies for bond issue.</title>
<headline>China Airlines applies for bond issue.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan carrier China Airlines said on Thursday it had applied to the Securities and Exchange Commission to issue T$3.5 billion in seven-year convertible bonds to raise funds for aircraft purchases.</p>
<p>The issue is China Airlines' first of convertible bonds, a company statement said.</p>
<p>In May, the airline signed contracts to buy eight Boeing 747-400s at a total cost of US$1.4 billion.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
